  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nCentral Idea: We develop a multi-scale optimization algorithm that uses both continuous and combinatorial phases to escape local optima. The algorithm alternates between smooth optimization and targeted binary randomization to find a function configuration that minimizes the maximum shift-overlap integral. This approach combines the stability of continuous relaxation with the exploration power of combinatorial perturbations, addressing the non-convex challenges of the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem.\n\nKey Innovation: The core novelty lies in the introduction of a \"Semi-Gradient Descent\" technique that gradually applies derivatives calculated via finite differences to both continuous and binary variables. This allows for both fine-tuning and exploration while maintaining the essential properties of the overlap metric.\n\nBottlenecks Addressed: This approach directly tackles the limitations of standard SLSQP by:\n- Reducing local trapping through adaptive binary randomization\n- Incorporating learning mechanisms from reinforcement algorithms\n- Maintaining a structured approach to shift-exploration\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\nVariables Representation:\n- Continuous representation: h \u2208 \u211d\u207f with 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i, \u2211h[i] = n/2\n- Binary representation: h \u2208 {0,1}\u207f with same constraints\n\nObjective Function:\n- C\u2085 = max\u2096 \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n- Discretized by: np.max(np.correlate(h,1-h,mode=\"full\")) * dx\n\nConstraints:\n1. Integral: \u2211h[i] = n/2 (transformed to integer counting by the solver)\n2. Bounds: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n\nAlgorithm Structure:\nPhase1: Continuous Optimization\n  - Smooth descent for all variables\n  - Gradient-based refinement\n  - CIll Compute deltas via finite differences\nPhase2: Mixed-Restricted Optimization\n  - Keeps top P solve results at any time\n  - Introduces fixed-rate binary randomization\n  - Minimizes only the top quantiles\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\nInitialization:\n  - Start with initial_h_values if available\n  - Convert to/project feasibility for current n\n  - Augment with bootstrapped samples\n\nComputation Management:\n  - Track current budget with budget_s\n  - Define global optimizer function:\n    def _optimize(h0, n, deadline):\n        results = []\n        # Main loop until deadline override\n        x0 = np.copy(h0)\n        x0_continuous = np.copy(h0) * 0.7 + 0.3 * np.random.rand(len(x0))\n        x0_binary = x0.copy()\n        # Target the current n-set of conditions\n        # Phase1: Smooth optimization for 40% budget\n        # Phase2: Autoencoder-style refinement for 30%\n        # Phase3: Noisy recovery with stratified sampling\n\nObjective Function Wrap:\n  - Adaptable compute_obj(x, n) compatible with:\n    - Gradient calculation via center differences\n    - Integral constraint handling\n  - Returns [C\u2085, -gradient, None] for SLSQP input\n\nConstraint Handling:\n  - Homogeneous bounds [0,1] for all variables\n  - Integral use separate penalization term\n  - def compute_obj(x): # Return losses and derivatives\n\nSolver Parameters:\n  - SLSQP's normal settings but pinned to:\n    - maxiter = 200\n    - ftol = 1e-6\n    - disp = False\n\nPhase Management:\n  - Time budgeted phases:\n    1. Discovery (35%): Brief gradient descent\n    2. Intensification (35%): Capped recursive refinement\n    3. Verification (30%): Forced binary normalized\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\nDefault Configuration:\n  - Multi-sdk SLSQP for continuous passes\n  - Binary stratification followed by \n  - Perturbation amplitude: 0.05 - 0.15\n  - step_size heuristic:  floor sqrt(n)/3 to adaptive scaling\n\nEscalation from Base:\n  - Solve-time adaptation by:\n    - Score-based iteration budget\n    - Mobile restarting on diversity depletion\n    - Dimensionality management: Keep n_base=250 fixed\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\nRuntime Estimation:\n  - Primary resolution (n=250): ~150 seconds\n  - Optimization depth: 4 nested levels per call\n  - Final-stage validation: Full 2*n-1 correlation\n\nDeadline Enforcement:\n  - Sub-budget per phase (e.g., 80 seconds total)\n  - Time-based acceptance check:\n    - monitor elapsed vs deadline\n  - Graceful degradation:\n    - Lower n-point set for speed\n    - Cooldown to S_optimal\n\nFinal Backup:\n  - Stores all viable candidates at \u2265 C\u2084\u2085\n  - Maintains a rolling average of: Top_score, n_ages\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\nImmediate Checks:\n  - Confirmed n even (enforcing integral feasibility)\n  - Score = np.max(correlation) * dx\n  - Post-check: \n    \u00b2  np.all((h[i]\u22650 and h[i]\u22641 for each i))\n    \u00b3  np.isinf(C5) ? Skip\n\nStatus Reporting:\n  - Structure:\n    [h, C5, n]\n    where C5 = best C\u2085 found\n\nException Handling:\n  - Zero-divergence via restarts\n  - Failsafe:\n    - Use n_base=250 fallback\n    - Compute C\u2085 again via np.correlate if divergence",
